---
description: >-
  Do not git push (or force-push) unless the current user message explicitly
  asks to push. Commit is not push. Prior confirmation does not carry over.
alwaysApply: true
---

# Git remotes (canon)

- Run `git push`, `git push --force`, `--force-with-lease`, or any other update of a remote branch only when **this** user message explicitly says to push.
- A request to **commit**, stage, or “save” is not permission to push.
- A “yes” from an earlier turn does not carry over. If the write would help but is not confirmed, say what you would push and wait.
